## Quick start

```bash
# Local dev with Postgres in Docker
docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up

# Or run without containers (you'll need Postgres on localhost)
cp .env.example .env
npm install
npm run dev
```

The service listens on `:3000`. Health check: `GET /healthz`. Readiness: `GET /readyz`.

## Scripts

| Script | What it does |
|---|---|
| `npm start` | Run the service in production mode |
| `npm run dev` | Run with auto-reload (nodemon) |
| `npm test` | Run Jest with coverage; fails below {{ coverage_threshold }}% |
| `npm run lint` | ESLint over `src/` and `tests/` |

## Layout

```
.
├── Dockerfile                # multi-stage build, distroless runtime
├── docker-compose.dev.yml    # local dev: this service + Postgres
├── .devcontainer/            # VS Code remote dev
├── .github/workflows/ci.yml  # GitHub Actions: lint, test, build, scan
├── azure-pipelines.yml       # Azure DevOps equivalent
├── src/index.js              # service entrypoint
├── tests/                    # Jest + Supertest
├── .env.example              # all env vars, no plaintext secrets
└── .gitleaks.toml            # secrets scanning config
```

